- In-place rewrite on the C++ backend (T4, issue #23).  Every return of
  generated code and every boxed primitive result did _0->forward_to(new
  node): it allocated the result and left a forward node in the redex, and
  every consumer compressed the chain and dispatched again.  The Python
  backend rewrites in place (node.py rewrite) and forwards only a reference
  result.  Done: Node::rewrite(info, args...) writes the info table and the
  successors of the result into the redex and returns the tag of the result;
  the arguments are read into locals before the first slot is written,
  because an argument may be a successor of the redex (swap x y = (y, x)).
  The generator (vEmit_compileS_IReturn) emits it when the block of the
  result fits the block of the redex, both computed from the arities as the
  info tables spell them (sizeof(Head) + sizeof(Arg[max(1, arity)]);
  InfoTable asserts the lower bound), and _0->forward_to as before when the
  result is larger, a partial application, or a pinned nullary constructor
  (Nil, Unit, True, False, Fail: the collector takes a node with a pinned
  info table for the static object and would never mark a heap copy).  A
  literal result is written as its info table and value, not as a new node.
  A reference result goes through Node::forward_or_copy: the redex is
  forwarded to the node, unless the node is an Int, Char, or Float, whose
  two words are copied (such a node is never rewritten, so a copy is as good
  as the node).  The primitives of unboxed.def write their boxed result into
  the redex; a Bool result is pinned and keeps the forward node.  apply
  writes the function node of a completed partial application into the
  redex when it fits (a function of up to two arguments;
  Node::rewrite_from_partial shares its filler with from_partial).  The
  rotation and collection cadence moved from the forward-chain compressions
  (the T_FWD cases of procD, procN, and hnf) into procS: a completed step
  counts and calls check_interrupts, so stepcount counts steps, the
  rotation runs every 65536 steps, and the stress mode of the collector
  collects after every step as before.  E_RESTART passes the check
  unchanged: it is counted by every enclosing procS on its way out, and a
  replacement by E_GC at the innermost level dropped those counts in stress
  mode (queens of CxxGc.curry counted 3068 steps against 3500).  hnf follows
  a chain of in-place tail calls under one scan frame (a do-while on
  T_FUNC).  The step binding of the Python API (InfoTable.step) refuses a
  node of another info table, because the step may write into the block.
  Audit of cursors into the redex across a rewrite: hnf still forwards its
  own results (a failure, a lifted constraint, a pull-tabbed choice), so
  the check in _applyspecial (_0->info->tag == T_FWD) stands; the trace
