  directory of the module to the path and both commands import the loaded
  module), sprite-exec -g, and on the Python backend saved modules: save
  refuses a goal the table cannot default and, without a goal, refuses to
  write a program (pass module_main=False for a library); the footer gains
  goalscheme=<FlatCurry type text> and moduleMain builds the goal from it,
  so the saved program runs from any directory.  save also compiles from
  the ICurry-JSON of a module whose loaded ICurry is a bill of materials
  (IExempt bodies): the saved file had a failing stub for every function,
  the known failure of examples/04-static-compile, now removed.  The text
  route lifts a trailing "where x, y free" to parameters of
  compiled_expression, as the REPL does (splitWhereFree), applies the
  goal to fresh free variables, and evaluates the tuple of the value and
  the variables; curry.eval yields Bindings objects that print as PAKCS
  prints them, {xs=[1, 2]} True, with one naming of the unbound variables
  across the parts; with exprtype the clause stays local.  compile.py also
  adds the root of a file module to the search path of an expression that
